How much correct is this: Native lazy loading: <img src="image.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="Description">
Google can discover the image from the src attribute without needing to scroll to it.
- JavaScript lazy loading: If the image URL is added to src only after scrolling or a JavaScript event, search engines may not discover it reliably.
